---
description: GitHub Actions baseline — SHA-pinned actions, OIDC, least-privilege.
globs: .github/workflows/**/*.yml,.github/workflows/**/*.yaml
alwaysApply: false
---

- ALWAYS pin actions to a 40-char SHA: `uses: actions/checkout@<sha>  # v4.1.7`.
- ALWAYS set `permissions:` to least-privilege (default `permissions: { contents: read }`, elevate per-job).
- ALWAYS use OIDC for cloud auth — NEVER long-lived static cloud keys in CI.
- NEVER `echo` a secret; mark derived outputs with `::add-mask::`.
- ALWAYS set `concurrency:` and `timeout-minutes:` on long-running jobs.
- NEVER `pull_request_target` with checkout of PR code unless you understand the supply-chain risk.
